The static locals and their guards: cxx1 spells a static local `count.s` and its guard `count.s$guard` where cl writes ?s@?1??count@@YAHH@Z@4US@@A and ?$TSS0@?1??count@@YAHH@Z@4HA - the divergence docs/CONFORMANCE.md records under "A static local keeps its own name in the object file", now with a guard beside it. File-local symbols, nothing links against them. And _Init_thread_abort, which cl calls from the unwind path if the constructor throws while the guard is held: cxx1 emits no such path yet, recorded in docs/CONFORMANCE.md.
